# Scratch queue rows CCO (plan_process_overhaul.md P2.1). Data: the queue table in scratch_queue.md is generated
# from this file (python3 tools/status_index.py). Format: tools/scratch_query/qrows.py docstring.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT feature_writeup/testing/rows/CCO.qb RES [--section KEY] [--rows ID,...]

@@section 1
@@title SQ-CCO Creative Common with its optional mods only: every Common tweak of a third-party mod, no Compat, no Calendar, no other Creative jar, 2026-11-07 ([creative_engineering.md](../creative_engineering.md) 7.1, `CommonMixinPlugin` NEEDS_MOD / MOD_RANGE)
@@date 2026-11-07
@@jars creativecommon creativeengineering
@@sources feature_writeup/creative_engineering.md
@@modset cc_only full
@@text
@@text Not run. Targets the newest `development/creativeCommon/build/libs/creativecommon-*.jar` (prep_srv.sh swaps it in when newer than `mods/`).
@@text Every server is built with `bash tools/scratch_query/cc_only_srv.sh OUT LEVEL full|alone|without=<keys> [prop=value ...]`:
@@text Common plus the KubeJS stack (KubeJS, Rhino, Architectury) plus the optional mods in the set, and nothing else (the script
@@text fails if another Creative jar is left; config/, defaultconfigs/ and the pack's kubejs/ are emptied so Common writes its own
@@text defaults). Optional mods covered: Immersive Weathering (+ Moonlight), Armor Trims, WorldEdit, Quark (+ AutoRegLib), Create
@@text Gravity (+ Create), Nock Enough Arrows, Better Beacons, Immersive Portals, Heartstone, Serene Seasons (portal overwrite
@@text conform). Keys: `iw trims we quark gravity nea beacons portals heartstone seasons`. If the first `full` boot reports a missing
@@text library for one mod (Create Gravity needs Create's own libraries), add it to `LIBS` in the script and note it in the run doc.
@@text Boot 1 `full` runs `batches/r1107cco/b1_full.qb` (SQ-CCO-01 to -04); the rest are console steps. Pack-config comparisons
@@text copy `configs_edited/root_config/creativecommon-common.toml` over the generated file. A `-` in Group means the row reuses the boot named.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-CCO-01 | no mixin or class error, every optional mod's mixins applied, no other Creative jar loaded
@group `full`, B
@commands the section's `@@modset cc_only full` (was `cc_only_srv.sh cco1 cco1 full spawn-monsters=true`), boot; batch b1_full.qb
@pass no `Mixin apply failed`, class error or out-of-range WARN; the Immersive Weathering `callTick ... now calls IwGrowthFast.blockTick`, Immersive Portals `overwrites conform` and Heartstone priority lines are present; no Creative jar name in the log apart from Common; 0 KubeJS startup errors; `creativecommon: N files loaded`
@fails `CommonMixinPlugin` tables, a dict key or startup file reaching a removed jar (Compat, Engineering)
@from batches/r1107cco/b1_full.qb
# 'Error loading class' WARNs are third-party mixin configs probing absent mods (Quark -> Lootr ConfigManager): not ours
bootreject Mixin apply failed|InvalidMixinException|outside the tested range|^(?!.*Error loading class).*(ClassNotFoundException|NoClassDefFoundError)
# a Creative item id inside a config default list (creativedelight:treated_stick_tomatoes in idleRandomTickRules) is not a jar: skip ids followed by ':'
bootreject (creativecompat|creativecalendar|creativeengineering|creativeequipment|creativemagic|creativedelight|creativebrewing)(?!:)
bootexpect \[perf\] Immersive Weathering callTick handler .* now calls IwGrowthFast\.blockTick
bootexpect \[compat\] Immersive Portals overwrites conform to target visibility
# the Heartstone priority line is client-only (orderHeartstoneBeforePortals returns on a dedicated server): CQ-CCO-01
# the scratch creativedevtools jar's own create/sequence_assembly_processes.js errors on recipe types of mods this set lacks: not Common
kjsreject ^(?!.*creativedevtools:kubejs/create/).*(?i:error)
look Done( \(|) line present, the Common startup files loaded line (`creativecommon: N files loaded`) in logs/kubejs/startup.log

## SQ-CCO-02 | Better Beacons present: its potions registered; effects work with only Common
@group -
@commands batch: Magic Resistance and Phantom Bane effects on a bot; no `[CE potions] ... not present` line
@pass both effects apply; Better Beacons' potions registered (`/give @p minecraft:potion{Potion:"creativecommon:magic_resistance"}` resolves)
@fails `CommonPotions` row `needsMod`, effect registration
@from batches/r1107cco/b1_full.qb passed
> pbot spawn s5pb1 0 70 0 minecraft:overworld creative
> effect give s5pb1 creativecommon:magic_resistance 30 0
> data get entity s5pb1 ActiveEffects
expect creativecommon:magic_resistance
> effect give s5pb1 better_beacons:phantom_bane 30 0
expect Applied effect Phantom Bane to s5pb1
reject (Unknown (item|block|block type|entity|effect)|Incorrect argument for command|No player was found|no such bot)
bootreject \[(CE|creativecommon) potions\] .* not present

## SQ-CCO-03 | WorldEdit present: the state-id skip does not break world edit
@group -
@commands batch: WorldEdit fill; `grep -c "WorldEdit" logs/latest.log`; time the `Done (` line against a boot with `without=we` (SQ-CCO-12)
@pass `//set` or fill works; no WorldEdit mixin error; `full` start is not slower by the WorldEdit state-table stall
@fails `WorldEditSkipStateIdInitMixin`, `WorldEditBlockStateIdAccessMixin`
@from batches/r1107cco/b1_full.qb
> execute at s5pb1 run fill ~ 69 ~ ~4 69 ~4 minecraft:stone
> execute at s5pb1 run say CCO03 fill done
expect CCO03 fill done
bootreject WorldEditSkipStateId|BlockStateIdAccess
look //pos1 and //set stone from the console is not possible (needs a player); run //set with the bot or a client when a window is up, else the fill above stands as the check

## SQ-CCO-04 | Common's default config is written fresh, no pack lists
@group -
@commands batch: default config; `grep -nE "overrides\|removed" config/creativecommon-common.toml`
@pass file written; `[mod_names] overrides = []`, `[effects] removed = []`, `[advancements] enabled = true`, `[creative_menu] disabled = false`, `[perf] gravityLimitDimensions = true`
@fails `CommonConfig` defaults
@from batches/r1107cco/b1_full.qb
shell grep -nE "^\s*(overrides|removed|gravityLimitDimensions|enabled|disabled) =" config/creativecommon-common.toml
shell test -f config/creativecommon-common.toml && echo CCO04 config present
look shell.txt: config present and overrides = [], removed = [], gravityLimitDimensions = true, [advancements] enabled = true, [creative_menu] disabled = false (the shell output is not in the server log)

## SQ-CCO-05 | Immersive Weathering fast random tick: no ASM warning, moss still spreads
@group -
@commands Immersive Weathering: `grep -E "IwGrowth\|callTick\|ServerLevelMixin" logs/latest.log`; `/gamerule randomTickSpeed 300`, place a stone block next to water and moss, `/time add 2400`, wait 60 s, count growth (moss, cracked, mossy variants) in a `/fill`-ed 32x32 stone slab with `/execute store result score ... run clone` or `/zq` block count
@pass no ASM warning (`unknown signature`, `handler not found`); growth still happens (block variants change) with the fast path; with `-Dcreativecommon.iwFastTick=false` in `srv/user_jvm_args.txt` the second boot logs `random-tick fast path off` and growth still happens
@fails `IwServerLevelTickMixin`, `IwGrowthFast`, IW 1.2.10 `callTick` signature
@from batches/r1107cco/b2_console.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootreject (?i)unknown signature|handler not found
bootexpect \[perf\] Immersive Weathering callTick handler .* now calls IwGrowthFast\.blockTick
> pbot remove-all
sleep 2
> pbot spawn s5pb1 0 70 0 minecraft:overworld creative
> forceload add 0 0 31 31
> fill 8 66 8 23 68 23 minecraft:stone
> fill 8 69 8 23 69 23 minecraft:cobblestone
> fill 8 70 8 23 72 23 minecraft:air
> setblock 15 69 15 minecraft:mossy_cobblestone
> setblock 16 70 16 minecraft:water
> cdevtest count 8 69 8 23 69 23 minecraft:mossy_cobblestone
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 300
> cdevtest tickwarp 1200
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done 120
> cdevtest count 8 69 8 23 69 23 minecraft:mossy_cobblestone
> cdevtest count 8 69 8 23 69 23 minecraft:cobblestone
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
look mossy_cobblestone count after 1200 ticks at randomTickSpeed 300 (tick warp: real level ticks, so the IW fast path runs; /cdevtest randomtick would bypass it) is higher than the first count (growth happens with the fast path)
expect verb=count block=minecraft:mossy_cobblestone n=[1-9]
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=\S+ .*error=

