## SQ-CCO-10 | Better Beacons Phantom Bane on the first player skips only that player (/zph, fresh spawner passes)
@group -
@commands Better Beacons phantom: `batches/r1107cc/b1_phantom.qb` (or `/zph N` with `cc_phantom_probe.js`); bots on y 70 platforms, `spawn-monsters=true`
@pass the second bot still gets phantoms while the first holds Phantom Bane (SQ-CC-10b on this set)
@fails `PhantomSpawnerBaneSkipMixin`
@from batches/r1107cco/b2_console.qb
> pbot remove-all
sleep 2
> effect clear s5pb1
> time set 18000
# the set boots peaceful: no phantom spawns at all (the probe prints difficulty=PEACEFUL)
> difficulty normal
# platforms in unloaded chunks are not placed (bots then fall into caves with no sky): forceload first
> forceload add -208 -8 -192 8
> forceload add 192 -208 208 -192
> fill -202 149 -2 -198 149 2 minecraft:stone
> fill 198 149 -202 202 149 -198 minecraft:stone
> pbot spawn s5pb1 -200 150 0 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 2
> pbot spawn s5pb2 200 150 -200 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 5
> s5 rest s5pb1 1200000
> s5 rest s5pb2 1200000
> zph 10
sleep 3
> execute at s5pb1 if entity @e[type=minecraft:phantom,distance=..80] run say CCO10C phantom near bot 1
> execute at s5pb2 if entity @e[type=minecraft:phantom,distance=..80] run say CCO10C phantom near bot 2
expect CCO10C phantom near bot 1
expect CCO10C phantom near bot 2
> kill @e[type=minecraft:phantom]
> effect give s5pb1 better_beacons:phantom_bane 9999
sleep 2
> zph 10
sleep 3
> execute at s5pb2 if entity @e[type=minecraft:phantom,distance=..80] run say CCO10 phantom near bot 2
> execute at s5pb1 if entity @e[type=minecraft:phantom,distance=..80] run say CCO10 phantom near bot 1
expect CCO10 phantom near bot 2
reject CCO10 phantom near bot 1
> kill @e[type=minecraft:phantom]
> time set noon
> difficulty peaceful
> forceload remove -208 -8 -192 8
> forceload remove 192 -208 208 -192
> pbot remove-all
reject (No player was found|no such bot|Unknown or incomplete command)

## SQ-CCO-11 | Immersive Portals + Serene Seasons + Heartstone on a server: conform line once, Nether trip
@group -
@commands Immersive Portals + Serene Seasons + Heartstone: `grep -E "overwrites conform\|Static binding violation\|Heartstone LevelRendererMixin priority" logs/latest.log`; `/execute in minecraft:the_nether run tp <bot> 0 100 0` and back; world join with a bot
@pass the conform line and the Heartstone priority line each appear once; no `cannot reduce visibility`; the Nether trip and the return do not crash
@fails `conformPortalsOverwrites`, `orderHeartstoneBeforePortals`, `imm_ptl.mixins.json` name
@from batches/r1107cco/b2_console.qb
shell grep -c "overwrites conform" logs/latest.log; grep -c "cannot reduce visibility\|Static binding violation" logs/latest.log; true
> pbot spawn s5pb1 0 70 0 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 2
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run tp s5pb1 0 100 0
sleep 8
> execute in minecraft:overworld run tp s5pb1 0 80 0
sleep 5
reject (?i)exception|crash
# one "Static binding violation ... visibility will be upgraded" for MixinChunkMap_C is the designed result of the conform
bootreject ^(?!.*Static binding violation).*cannot reduce visibilit|InvalidMixinException
look conform count 1, Static binding violation count 1 (designed, MixinChunkMap_C upgraded); the Heartstone priority line is client-only (CQ-CCO-01)

## SQ-CCO-12 | (split into SQ-CCO-12a to -12f, one per mod set)
@group B
@superseded split into SQ-CCO-12a to -12f, one row per cco_sets variant (r1118 R4 B1, 2026-11-18): each set is its own step and world

## SQ-CCO-12a | without_we: boots, reloads and stops clean; absent mods' mixins skipped, effects still work
@group B (cco_sets without_we: cc_only full without we)
@commands boot; `grep -E "Mixin apply failed\|InvalidMixinException\|ClassNotFoundException\|NoClassDefFoundError\|outside the tested range" logs/latest.log`; `grep -c ERROR logs/kubejs/startup.log`; `/reload`; `/effect give <bot> creativecommon:magic_resistance 30 0`
@pass each boots, reloads and stops clean; the skipped mod's mixins are not applied and not an error; only `without=beacons` logs `[CE potions] better_beacons not present - skipping` (if that row is guarded by it) and Phantom Bane is absent; the rest still work
@fails missing `NEEDS_MOD` row, a Java or script path reaching the absent mod
@from batches/r1107cco/b4_without.qb
@modset cco_sets without_we
# r1118 R4 B1 (2026-11-18): one of the six SQ-CCO-12 sets; its own step and world (the old "reuse level cco1" does not hold)
bootreject Mixin apply failed|InvalidMixinException|outside the tested range|^(?!.*Error loading class).*(ClassNotFoundException|NoClassDefFoundError)
bootreject (?i)creativecommon.*(exception|error)
# generators-and-tests #28 (2026-11-22): the Devtools sequenced assembly test recipe adds each mod's steps only when it is loaded
kjsreject sequence_assembly_processes\.js#\d+: Failed
shell grep -E "creativecommon: .* files loaded" logs/kubejs/startup.log; grep -c "ERROR" logs/kubejs/startup.log || true
shell grep -E "\[CE potions\]|\[perf\]|\[compat\]" logs/latest.log | sed -E 's/^.*\]: //' | head -10
shell grep -oE "Mixing [A-Za-z_.]+ from creativecommon[^ ]* into [A-Za-z_.$]+" logs/debug.log 2>/dev/null | awk '{print $2}' | sort -u | head -40 || true
> pbot spawn s5pb1 0 120 0 minecraft:overworld creative
> reload
sleep 20
> effect give s5pb1 creativecommon:magic_resistance 30 0
> effect give s5pb1 better_beacons:phantom_bane 30 0
sleep 1
reject (?i)/ERROR\].*creativecommon
expect Applied effect Magic Resistance to s5pb1
> pbot remove-all
look KubeJS startup ERROR count 0 (or only absent-mod notes); [CE potions] skip line only when Better Beacons is out (and Phantom Bane give then fails as an unknown effect); Common mixins listed target only mods in the set

